# Close sessions

`--close` should kill only a strictly resolved live tmux session and preserve
all jj workspace state and checkout directories.

    :bins jj tmux cat sh sed test

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'sh', 'sed', and 'test' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name feature alpha.feature (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name other alpha.other (exit: 0)

Create repo-backed sessions for the default and both named workspaces, plus a
plain session that collides with the natural feature tmux name.

    :t new-session -d -s alpha/feature "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha/feature~1 -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=alpha/feature~1:' @smth.repo '#{pane_current_path}' (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha/other -c alpha.other "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=alpha/other:' @smth.repo '#{pane_current_path}' (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha-live -c alpha "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=alpha-live:' @smth.repo '#{pane_current_path}' (success)
    :t new-session -d -s scratch "cat" (success)

A named-workspace base should infer `feature` and close the disambiguated
repo-backed session while leaving the colliding plain session alive.

    :$ smth --base alpha.feature --close (exit: 0)
    :t has-session -t '=alpha/feature~1' (failure)

```
can't find session: alpha/feature~1
```

    :t has-session -t '=alpha/feature' (success)
    :$ test -d alpha.feature (exit: 0)
    :$ sh -c 'jj workspace list -R alpha --ignore-working-copy --no-pager --color never --template "name ++ \"\\n\"" | sed -n "/feature/p"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
feature
```

An explicit operand overrides the inferred workspace, and omitting the operand
for a default base closes the default checkout's live session.

    :$ smth --base alpha.feature --close other (exit: 0)
    :t has-session -t '=alpha/other' (failure)

```
can't find session: alpha/other
```

    :$ test -d alpha.other (exit: 0)

    :$ smth --base alpha --close (exit: 0)
    :t has-session -t '=alpha-live' (failure)

```
can't find session: alpha-live
```

    :$ test -d alpha (exit: 0)

The plain namespace remains independent: it can close both an ordinary plain
session and the plain collision without consulting repository metadata.

    :$ smth --no-base --close scratch (exit: 0)
    :t has-session -t '=scratch' (failure)

```
can't find session: scratch
```

    :$ smth --no-base --close alpha/feature (exit: 0)
    :t has-session -t '=alpha/feature' (failure)

```
can't find session: alpha/feature
```

Closing a registered workspace with no live session fails safely, as does an
unspecified plain target.

    :$ smth --base alpha --repo "alpha*" --close feature (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session is not live
```

    :$ smth --no-base --close (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session not found
```

Close rejects picker controls and every other lifecycle action.

    :$ smth --no-base --close runner --query runner (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--close [<SESSION>]' cannot be used with '--query <STR>'

Usage: smth --no-base --close [<SESSION>]

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --no-base --close runner --create runner (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--close [<SESSION>]' cannot be used with '--create [<SESSION>]'

Usage: smth --no-base --close [<SESSION>]

For more information, try 'help'.
```

